5. Resource-Vector Partial Order and Simultaneous Confidence Bands

5.1 Formal partial order

Let \mathcal{R} = \mathbb{R}_{+}^k denote the resource space, with \mathbf{R} = (r_1,\dots,r_k) tracking computational expenditure. Let \mathcal{K} = \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}^k be the positive orthant. For \mathbf{R}_a, \mathbf{R}_b \in \mathcal{R}, \mathbf{R}_a \preceq_{\mathcal{K}} \mathbf{R}_b if and only if r_{a,j} \le r_{b,j} for all j. The baseline frontier at operating point \mathbf{R} is

P^*(T,\mathbf{R}) = \sup_{b \in \mathcal{B}} \sup_{\mathbf{R}' \preceq_{\mathcal{K}} \mathbf{R}} \mathbb{E}[P(b,T,\mathbf{R}')],

which guarantees monotonicity: if \mathbf{R}_1 \preceq_{\mathcal{K}} \mathbf{R}_2, then P^*(T,\mathbf{R}_1) \le P^*(T,\mathbf{R}_2).

5.2 Ray-to-convex-hull positivity

Let \mathcal{U} = \{\mathbf{u}_1,\dots,\mathbf{u}_m\} \subset \mathbb{S}^{k-1} \cap \mathbb{R}_{+}^k be a finite generating set of unit rays spanning cone \mathcal{C} = \mathrm{cone}(\mathcal{U}). Suppose the coordination premium \Pi(G,T,\mathbf{R}) satisfies strict positivity on generating rays and either concavity in \mathbf{R} or L-Lipschitz continuity with mesh radius h < \delta/L. Then \Pi(G,T,\mathbf{R}) > 0 uniformly for every \mathbf{R} in the truncated convex hull. This resolves the ambiguity of statements about positivity “across the resource vector” and prevents sign reversals between tested budget rays.

Formal status. [D], conditional on the stated concavity or Lipschitz condition.

5.3 Simultaneous confidence bands

Because both \hat{P}(G,T,\mathbf{R}) and \hat{P}^*(T,\mathbf{R}) are random, pointwise intervals fail to control family-wise error across the continuous resource domain \mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{R}}. Under Donsker regularity, the empirical process \mathbb{G}_N(\mathbf{R}) = \sqrt{N}(\hat{\Pi}_N(\mathbf{R}) - \Pi(\mathbf{R})) converges weakly to a tight centered Gaussian process. The Gaussian multiplier bootstrap band is

\mathcal{C}_{1-\alpha}(\mathbf{R}) = \left[ \hat{\Pi}_N(\mathbf{R}) - c_{1-\alpha}^* \frac{\hat{\sigma}_N(\mathbf{R})}{\sqrt{N}}, \;\; \hat{\Pi}_N(\mathbf{R}) + c_{1-\alpha}^* \frac{\hat{\sigma}_N(\mathbf{R})}{\sqrt{N}} \right],

where c_{1-\alpha}^* is the empirical (1-\alpha)-quantile of the supremum of the multiplier process. The band satisfies asymptotically uniform coverage:

\lim_{N \to \infty} \mathbb{P}\!\left( \Pi(G,T,\mathbf{R}) \in \mathcal{C}_{1-\alpha}(\mathbf{R}) \;\; \forall \mathbf{R} \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{R}} \right) = 1 - \alpha.

Formal status. [V] for the Gaussian multiplier bootstrap methodology for simultaneous bands; [D] for the specialization to the coordination-premium process.

The operational rule is that a network passes the coordination-premium criterion if and only if

\inf_{\mathbf{R} \in \mathcal{G}_{\mathcal{R}}} \left( \hat{\Pi}_N(\mathbf{R}) - c_{1-\alpha}^* \frac{\hat{\sigma}_N(\mathbf{R})}{\sqrt{N}} \right) > 0.

