8. Evidence Profile, States, and Falsification

8.1 Evidence profile

D(G) = (\mathbf{C}, \mathbf{S}, \mathbf{K}, \mathbf{T}, \mathbf{R}, \mathbf{U}),

where \mathbf{C} is the capability vector, \mathbf{S} the synergy-gate evidence, \mathbf{K} the edge-level causal contribution profile with sham subtraction and false-discovery-rate control, \mathbf{T} the transfer evidence at T1/T2/T3, \mathbf{R} the fragility vector, and \mathbf{U} the uncertainty statement.

8.2 Evidence states

· S0: \Pi \le 0 at the preregistered primary resource match.
· S1: \Pi > 0 but the synergy gate is not passed, or transfer is limited to T1.
· S2: synergy gate passed, \Pi > 0 at the primary match and at T2, and the bifactor F retains incremental predictive validity over M.
· S3: all of S2, plus positive genuine edge contributions for a preregistered fraction of edges, plus positive T3 transfer, plus lower fragility than B_{\mathrm{ens}} on a preregistered subset of perturbations.

S3 is not equivalent to confirmed AGI. It is a designation for further scientific investigation.

8.3 Falsification criteria

· F1 — No transfer advantage: \Delta_{\mathrm{transfer}}^{(2)} or \Delta_{\mathrm{transfer}}^{(3)} not positive.
· F2 — Individual capability explains results: F fails incremental predictive validity over M.
· F3 — Computation explains results: B_{\mathrm{ens}} reproduces collective performance.
· F4 — Interaction unnecessary: \Gamma_e^{\mathrm{genuine}} not positive after false-discovery-rate control.
· F5 — No reproducibility: results fail to reproduce across configurations, generators, and evaluators.
· F6 — Narrow specialization: premium only on decomposable tasks.
· F7 — No synergy: gate not passed on T2 or T3 tasks.
· F8 — No discrimination: AUC confidence interval does not exclude 0.5 on the non-circular positive-adjacent versus negative control comparison.

F8 is the decisive falsification criterion: a framework that cannot discriminate known-synergistic from known-non-synergistic systems has no claim to detect the unknown.

