The empirical benchmark from the paired-protocol audit literature is that a carefully constructed format-matched placebo still produces a behavioral shift of approximately 4 percentage points relative to hidden delivery, versus 20 points for real delivery. A sham that produces a shift of this magnitude is detectable in principle; an audit that does not detect it is underpowered or using an insensitive discriminator.

